{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794750026,"nonce":"Ex7AMXRW3VTGdtQqaZktIyav6RM=","message":"First body lowering slice (commit after 1fafbfd9): numeric kernels go from the TAST to AIR, verify, and compute the right answers.\n\nCovers: i32, f64 and bool values; locals built into SSA as the body is walked (Braun et al.: blocks sealed when their predecessors are known, incomplete phis for reads in unsealed blocks, trivial phis removed); arithmetic, comparisons and int-to-float promotion; if as statement and as value; while, do-while, break and continue; return; \u0026\u0026 and || as conditions and as values; ++ and -- on locals; compound assignment; direct calls of static functions (call and definition ask the same function index). Anything else is refused with a message that names it, so no body is half lowered.\n\nCheck: 13 kernels (fib, sum, gcd, collatz, a float loop with int-to-float promotion, isPrime with early return, abs, clamp, a short-circuit bool value, do-while, while(true) with break, continue, nested for loops) lower to AIR, pass air::v2::verify, and a reference interpreter (ash_nair::eval) computes the same results as the same functions in Rust across many inputs. ASH_NAIR_DUMP=1 prints the AIR.\n\nThe IR is clean: fib is the direct recursive shape; loops have real loop-carried phis and continue is an explicit edge. Duplicate constants are left for GVN.\n\nNot yet: objects, fields, arrays, strings, closures, enums, try/catch, calls through instances or interfaces, anything that needs the runtime. Nothing runs on an engine yet: the AIR needs a module (type table, pools, function table) in the form the engines take, which is the next integration step. Specialized copies are not consumed yet either.","files":null}]}